# Scratch working files for this session. Ignored, not committed: `git clean -fd`
# does not touch ignored paths, which is what keeps them from being swept away.
.lavish-wip/

# Artifacts `omp` writes into the CWD when a run is exercised end-to-end from a
# scratch session (`omp session`, browser recording). They are output, not source:
# a `git add -A` in a repo root that has one on disk would commit a stray `.probe`
# and a pair of frames. Matched at the repo root so a real file of the same name
# deeper in the tree is still tracked.
/omp-session-*.md
/omp-session-*.markdown
/omp-session-*.probe
/omp-browser-recording-*/

# Scratch directories a throwaway probe gets written into. These keep recurring —
# `.probe`, then the session artifacts above, then `.scratch` — and each time the
# fix blocked exactly ONE instance. `bun test` scans `test/`, so an untracked
# scratch dir under it runs as a passing test that protects nothing, and a
# `git add -A` commits it. Matched at ANY depth: the location is the point, not
# the name, and a scratch dir is scratch wherever it is created.
**/.probe/
**/.scratch/
